  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"After counting returns, the team can divide spare cups between the lending station and a nearby reserve shelf.\", \"decision\": \"How should spare cups be positioned for the next gathering?\", \"goal\": \"Make cup lending and return convenient while keeping the available stock and volunteer work understandable.\", \"problem\": \"A neighborhood café wants to lend reusable cups at community gatherings and recover them afterward. It has a modest cup stock, washable collection crates, a simple lending record, and volunteers who can share short shifts. The plan concerns a small pilot with no deposit or sales system. Different decisions address separate moments in lending, return, and review.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nThe team starts with a modest lending-station stock and moves cups from the reserve shelf when the request list grows. The stock near guests follows demand during the event.\nThe team divides spare cups between the lending station and reserve shelf by the expected length of each service block. The initial placement reflects the planned service schedule.\nThe team uses the busiest previous service block to set the lending-station stock and puts the rest on the reserve shelf. The starting stock reflects observed peak demand."
    }
